# Comparing demosaic methods on the same sensor data.
#
# mosaic("test") is the undemosaiced sensor readout -- one sample per pixel,
# linear, at the sensor's full bit depth. image("test") would instead give the
# demosaiced result using the app's default method, which is what every other
# script gets without having to ask.
#
# Drop a raw file (.CR3, .CR2, .ARW, .NEF, ...) onto the "test" row.
# On a PNG or JPEG this script errors, deliberately: there is no mosaic to show.

raw = mosaic("test")

a = choose("method A", "demosaic", demosaic_ahd)
b = choose("method B", "demosaic", demosaic_malvar)

outA = params(a, "A")(raw)
outB = params(b, "B")(raw)

display(outA, "1 method A")
display(outB, "2 method B")

# Pick demosaic_passthrough in either dropdown to see the raw Bayer pattern
# itself -- zoom in and the colour filter array is visible, one colour per
# pixel, before any interpolation.
#
# demosaic_ahd is adaptive: it interpolates green ALONG edges rather than
# across them, so thin high-contrast detail -- bare branches against sky, wires,
# hair -- keeps its colour instead of breaking into coloured speckles. Against a
# known scene it scores 36.1 dB where Malvar scores 26.4, with five times less
# false colour.
#
# It is now the default that image() inserts. It was not, while it was CPU-only
# -- 22 s on a 45 MP frame against Malvar's single GPU dispatch. With a GPU path
# the two cost the same (495 ms against 509 ms), because at that size both are
# bound by memory bandwidth rather than arithmetic.
